# docs/orphans-allow — the meta-repo's EXPECTED live-orphan census (WI-228).
#
# Read by project-trajectory/scripts/check_docs.py. A "live orphan" is a doc no
# navigation path reaches from an entry root. Most of ours are RETAINED EVIDENCE
# — round reviews, closed-WI specs, dual-plan artifacts, generated indexes — that
# must stay on disk yet is not a navigation node: "unlinked-from-navigation" is
# the wrong frame for it. Each non-comment line is a shell glob (fnmatch, repo-
# relative POSIX; `*` spans separators, so `docs/reviews/*` covers the whole
# subtree). A matched orphan is EXPECTED — dropped from the per-doc warnings, an
# aggregate `note` in their place, and never a finding (even under
# --strict-orphans). An orphan matching NOTHING here is GENUINE: it warns (fails
# under --strict-orphans), the newly-introduced-orphan RATCHET — link/index it,
# or, if it is a new evidence class, add its glob here with a reason.
#
# WHY a census, not deletion-or-mass-indexing (repo-review-2026-07-18 M-07):
# deleting would destroy history; indexing everything would bloat navigation
# (status.md / README stay lean). This bounds the noise so a genuinely
# undiscoverable new doc no longer hides in 60-odd steady warnings — the same
# silent-growth mode the C901 ratchet (WI-225) bounds for complexity. (The
# duplication census bounded the third such mode until D-7/WI-426 deleted it;
# duplicated plumbing is unbounded by ruling now.) A GENUINE straggler is linked instead
# of listed: docs/specs/parallel-dispatch-design-notes.md is reached from its
# companion plan, so it is navigable and absent below.

# review evidence — the per-round Reviewer/Critique/Grounding artifacts and the
# top-level whole-repo reviews; kept as the audit trail, referenced from log.md.
docs/reviews/*
# (docs/repo-review-*.md glob retired 2026-08-13w — the root repo-reviews moved
# to docs/archive/history/, which check_docs exempts structurally.)

# re-attestation briefs — the per-SITTING instrument `trace.py --ratify modified`
# generates and `ratify-fresh` gates: the owner reads the live one before blessing
# a `Modified` row, and finished ones stay as the record of what was shown. The
# same retained-evidence class as the round reviews above (WI-280 added the glob
# when it opened the first Modified window since the briefs began; earlier ones
# were reachable only incidentally, from whichever handoff doc happened to cite
# them, which is reachability by accident rather than by class).
docs/ratify/*

# log fragments awaiting the serial trunk step — a work branch's docs/log.md
# entry, parked under its own unique name until trunk_step.py compiles it into
# the log (concurrency-restructure.md §5.1). Transient by construction and never
# a navigation node: the entry becomes reachable the moment it lands in log.md.
docs/log.d/*

# work-item specs — the per-WI SpecRef files (open and closed). Registry-
# referenced (docs/requirements/work-items.csv), not doc-graph navigation nodes.
docs/specs/WI-*.md

# archived closed-WI specs — the WI-251 sweep's steady state: retained evidence,
# date-stamped + WI-attributed, reached from log.md entries not navigation.
docs/archive/specs/*

# dual-plan decomposition rounds — one directory per round plus the plans/ index;
# the verdict is summarized in log.md and selected rows are filed as real WIs.
docs/plans/*

# archived plan documents — the 2026-08-13 consolidation moved the spent/depth
# plan set (and the closed DP-001 round) under docs/archive/plans/, indexed by
# its README; same retained-evidence class as docs/archive/specs/*.
docs/archive/plans/*

# generated iteration-log index — freshness owned by its generator, not
# hand-navigated (the same "never lint generated output" stance as docs/okf/).
docs/iteration_index.md
